.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-PUBLISH-MESSAGE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-publish-message \- publish a message to a topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens publish-message
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I ERN
.BR \-\-body | \-b
.I BODY
[\fB\-\-attributes\fR|\fB\-a\fR \fIJSON\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes a message to a topic. If
.B \-\-body
starts with
.IR file:// ,
the message body is read from the referenced file instead of being
taken literally.
.PP
The optional
.B \-\-attributes
value sets the message attributes as a JSON object mapping attribute
name to
.IR "{\(dqtype\(dq: <int|long|double|float|bool|string|binary>, \(dqvalue\(dq: <value>}" ,
given either literally or via
.I file://path
to a file containing the JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the destination topic. Required.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-body " " \fIBODY\fR
Message body, given literally or as
.I file://path
to a file to read it from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attributes " " \fIJSON\fR
Message attributes as a JSON object, given literally or as
.I file://path
to a file to read it from. Optional.
.PP
The topic may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The message was published; its message ID and body/attribute MD5 sums
are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, a referenced
.I file://
path could not be read, or no topic with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens publish-message \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --body 'hello world'

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens publish-message \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --body file://./payload.json \e
    --attributes '{"orderId": {"type": "string", "value": "42"}}'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-create-topic (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-messages (1)
